    "# Quiz: Cuisine classifiers 2\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-3-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A good initial classifier to try is:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Linear SVC</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Following the classifier map for our data, the first classifier to try is a Linear SVC.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>K-Means</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Following the classifier map, the first classifier to try is a Linear SVC.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Logical SVC</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The classifier is called a Linear SVC, and it is the first one the map suggests.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-3-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Regularization controls:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>the influence of parameters</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The C parameter sets regularization, which regulates the influence of parameters.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>the influence of training speed</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Regularization, set with the C parameter, regulates the influence of parameters.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>the influence of outliers</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Regularization regulates the influence of parameters. You set it with the C parameter.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-3-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>K-Neighbors classifier can be used for:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>supervised learning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is true, but the neighbors family can be used for unsupervised learning too.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>unsupervised learning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is true, but the neighbors family can be used for supervised learning too.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of these</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. K-Neighbors belongs to the neighbors family, which can be used for both supervised and unsupervised learning.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
