   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-3-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Support-Vector classifiers can be used for</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>classification</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Support-vector methods are used for classification, but also for regression tasks.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>regression</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Support-vector methods are used for regression, but also for classification tasks.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of these</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Support-vector methods are used for both classification and regression tasks.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-3-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Random Forest is a ___ type of classifier</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Ensemble</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Random Forest is an ensemble classifier. Ensembles combine the predictions of several base estimators.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Dissemble</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Random Forest is an ensemble classifier. It builds a forest of decision trees.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Assemble</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The word is ensemble. Ensemble methods combine the predictions of several base estimators.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-4-3-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Adaboost is known for:</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>focusing on the weights of incorrectly classified items</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. AdaBoost focuses on the weights of incorrectly classified items and adjusts the next classifier to correct them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>focusing on outliers</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. AdaBoost focuses on the weights of items that were classified incorrectly, then adjusts the next fit.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>focusing on incorrect data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. AdaBoost focuses on items that were classified incorrectly, not on incorrect data, and adjusts the next fit to fix them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
